#### Side Band Background Estimation

In addition to the mixed-event method, a side band method is also used to crosscheck the results. Figure 4.6 shows results of this method, where the background is estimated from an average of the signal+background in a region just below and just above the observed peak in the signal+background. Here we assume that the background linearity is good. Regions \(B_{1}\) and \(B_{2}\) are chosen each to be half the width of region \(B_{0}\). So \(B_{0}\) can be approximated as \((B_{1}+B_{2})\). Further, we assume \(S_{1}\approx B_{1}\) and \(S_{2}\approx B_{2}\). Then the corrected yield is \(S_{0}-(S_{1}+S_{2})\). The results show excellent agreement between the mixed-event method and the side band method.

